  "notes": [
    "Divisional Commander, then 1 to 4 Infantry Brigades: 1 to 3 Infantry Regiments each (0-3 Line, 0-1 Light, 0-1 Foreign [Spanish/Portuguese/Rheinbund]). Max 10 battalions per brigade, max 1 Light regiment per division.",
    "0 to 1 Regimental Artillery section per two battalions, or 0 to 1 Regimental Artillery Battery per regiment of 3+ battalions.",
    "0 to 2 Light Cavalry Brigades (max 1 per 2 Infantry Brigades): 1 to 4 regiments from Hussars, Lancers, Chasseurs à Cheval, Polish Uhlans, Württemberg Horse-Jägers, Bavarian Chevaulegers.",
    "Divisional Artillery: up to 1 Foot battery (6+ battalions in army) and up to 1 Horse battery (3+ cavalry regiments) attach to any brigade.",
    "Corps and Army Support: up to 50% of points on Reserve Artillery, a Heavy Cavalry Brigade (if 2+ infantry brigades taken), and an Artillery Brigade (if 12+ infantry battalions taken).",
    "0 to 1 Heavy Cavalry Brigade (if 2 Infantry Brigades taken): 1 to 3 regiments of Carabiniers/Cuirassiers, or Dragoons, plus up to 1 Small Lancer regiment.",
    "Allies: a French army can take 25% allies from the Imperial Guard list, plus 25% from any other allied list."
  ]
